Gas-n-Go is a chain of auto body shops in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. Its shop at 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] is a small one-story building on a busy street of through traffic: gas pumps under an awning out front, a garage of three bays to one side, a counter and a store level inside, and alleys with dumpsters and a service door down the left side.

Under the shop, past a locked back door on the store level, is a [[Hearts|Heart]]'s fane, and none of it matches the shop above. A spiral stair turns counterclockwise between stained glass showing one continuous fire, the air is warm, and the floor and inner wall are dull steel plating with pneumatics moving beneath them, like the building breathing. The stair is narrow enough for one person at a time. At its foot, a steel-and-glass hall leads to a glass bridge over a gap, with a throne on a raised altar at the far end.

The [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] hid [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] in that fane. The Party's own car sat in one of the shop's bays on a hoist while the gang worked on it, and the Party found its keys on a rack by the counter before going down the stair.

Below the throne room the fane continues into a seven-sided antechamber, a door set in each of its six outer walls. In the center, a foot off the ground, a five-foot chunk of obsidian turns slowly clockwise, threaded with veins of stained glass that widen as they watch. The voice of the fane's [[Gas-n-Go Heart|Heart]] comes out of the rock.

Each door is a wrought-iron arch nine feet tall, fronted with stained glass. Behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]]'s door is Tywelwyn's bedroom, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s the armory, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]]'s the radar dish plant and the room where he prepared for the pilgrimage, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]]'s his office, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]]'s a haberdasher, and behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]]'s an orrery.

The bedroom holds a wide four-post bed with mirrors above it and a wardrobe of eight identical capes, alongside a black robe three sizes too large for Tywelwyn. The armory keeps firearms in lockers and shelves, and the gear the gang stripped from the Party's dead. The office is cramped and plain next to the rest of the fane: a typewriter, tables of papers, and wheeled chalkboards drawn with a map of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] and with musical notation. The Party took what papers and ledgers they could carry, and left the rest.
